    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0146" n="64" xml:id="pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.61334/175: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Boding</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-05-09T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1925—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>12. Department has received letter directly from Mercantile Bank of the Americas
                    stating that a settlement has been reached substantially as given in your 15,
                    May 6, 4 P.M.</p>
                <p>You should, however, continue to report promptly by cable any important
                    developments affecting this case.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d50-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d50-f1" n="10" xml:id="d50-f1-content">
                <p>On May 18, 4 p.m., the Minister informed the Department that an agreement between
                    the Mercantile Bank and the Association of Agriculturists had been signed on May
                    15 (file No. 822.61334/178).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
